lctech f1c200s: partition the on-board SPI NAND, and carry NAND bootargs

The board .dts declares the GigaDevice 128 MiB SPI NAND under &spi0 but defines
no partitions, so the chip enumerates as a single whole-device /dev/mtd0. That
was deliberate while all we wanted was a full-chip backup; installing to it
needs named partitions.

Mirrors the vendor layout exactly, read off the stock firmware's own /proc/mtd:

  0x00000000  512 KiB  u-boot
  0x00080000  5.5 MiB  kernel.itb    FIT (kernel + dtb)
  0x00600000   64 MiB  rom           squashfs, read-only  -> overlayfs lower
  0x04600000   48 MiB  overlay       jffs2,    read-write -> overlayfs upper

Leaving the last 10 MiB unpartitioned, as stock does. Mirroring rather than
inventing a layout means our artifacts are known to fit (measured: kernel.itb
4.54 MiB of 5.5 MiB, squashfs ~30 MiB of 64 MiB) and the stock backup maps onto
it 1:1 for restore.

CONFIG_MTD_OF_PARTS=y is already set in linux.fragment specifically to parse
this once it existed.

The second half of this patch is the non-obvious one. We keep the STOCK
bootloader in mtd0, because mainline U-Boot's SPL cannot boot SPI NAND on suniv
(board.c returns SUNXI_INVALID_BOOT_SOURCE for SUNIV_BOOTED_FROM_NAND). So the
kernel's command line on the NAND path is whatever that bootloader supplies --
and it supplies NOTHING. Its script is:

  nand_boot=echo "Booting from SPI-NAND..."; \
            mtd read spi-nand0 ${kernel_addr_r} 0x80000 0x580000; \
            bootm ${kernel_addr_r};

with kernel_addr_r=0x81000000, and its environment defines no "bootargs"
variable at all -- confirmed with strings(1) over the stock mtd0 dump. The
vendor gets its command line from the chosen node of the DTB inside its own
FIT; carving that DTB out of the stock mtd1 dump and decompiling it shows
exactly the string added here. So: no bootargs in the tree means an empty
kernel command line, no console, no root=, and a panic with nothing on the
serial line to explain it.

Adding it to chosen{} costs the SD path nothing. U-Boot's fdt_chosen()
overwrites chosen/bootargs whenever the "bootargs" env var is non-empty, and
our own U-Boot sets CONFIG_BOOTARGS, so on SD this property is replaced before
the kernel ever sees it. It takes effect precisely when the bootloader offers
nothing, which is the case it exists for.

Note this affects the SD image too -- one kernel and one .dts serve both -- so
an SD-booted system now sees /dev/mtd0..3 instead of a single mtd0. That is
wanted: the SD system is what flashes the NAND, and it should address the
partitions by name.

Signed-off-by: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c200s-lctech-pi.dts	2026-08-16 16:53:19.994210564 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c200s-lctech-pi.dts	2026-08-16 17:33:27.862016227 +0200
@@ -21,6 +21,33 @@
 
 	chosen {
 		stdout-path = "serial0:115200n8";
+
+		/*
+		 * Default cmdline for the SPI-NAND boot path. It has to live
+		 * HERE, in the device tree, because the on-board bootloader
+		 * passes none: its nand_boot is exactly
+		 *
+		 *   mtd read spi-nand0 ${kernel_addr_r} 0x80000 0x580000;
+		 *   bootm ${kernel_addr_r};
+		 *
+		 * and its environment defines no "bootargs" variable at all
+		 * (verified with strings(1) on the stock mtd0 dump). The
+		 * vendor's own FIT carries the identical string in its own
+		 * chosen node, which is where the running stock system's
+		 * /proc/cmdline came from. Without this the NAND boot reaches
+		 * the kernel with an EMPTY command line -- no console, no
+		 * root= -- and panics with nothing on the wire to explain it.
+		 *
+		 * The SD path is unaffected: our own U-Boot sets CONFIG_BOOTARGS,
+		 * and a non-empty "bootargs" env makes U-Boot's fdt_chosen()
+		 * overwrite this property before handing the tree to the kernel.
+		 * So this string is what runs iff the bootloader supplies nothing.
+		 *
+		 * musb_hdrc.use_dma=0 is deliberately NOT here -- CMDLINE_EXTEND
+		 * appends it to whichever of the two command lines wins, so it
+		 * cannot be lost by editing only one of them.
+		 */
+		bootargs = "console=ttyS0,115200 panic=5 rootwait init=/preinit root=/dev/mtdblock2 rootfstype=squashfs overlayfsdev=/dev/mtdblock3";
 	};
 
 	reg_vcc3v3: regulator-3v3 {
@@ -52,6 +79,32 @@
 		compatible = "spi-nand";
 		reg = <0>;
 		spi-max-frequency = <40000000>;
+
+		partitions {
+			compatible = "fixed-partitions";
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <1>;
+
+			partition@0 {
+				label = "u-boot";
+				reg = <0x000000 0x080000>;
+			};
+
+			partition@80000 {
+				label = "kernel.itb";
+				reg = <0x080000 0x580000>;
+			};
+
+			partition@600000 {
+				label = "rom";
+				reg = <0x600000 0x4000000>;
+			};
+
+			partition@4600000 {
+				label = "overlay";
+				reg = <0x4600000 0x3000000>;
+			};
+		};
 	};
 };
 
